# Figma Plugin UI Design Rules

Shared design authority:

- `.cursor/rules/shared-design-system.mdc`

This file defines plugin-specific constraints and **parity with the Chrome extension library**. If a local rule differs from shared guidance, mark it:

- `FigmaConstraint: <reason>`

---

# Extension Library Parity (Required)

The plugin UI must be **visually and structurally consistent** with the **Chrome extension library** (`chrome-extension/extension/src/library`, `chrome-extension/extension/src/popup/components/SnippetCard.tsx`, `SnippetLibrary.tsx`).

## Layout and structure

- **Header**: title (e.g. "Element Armory"), optional subtitle; search on the same row or directly below.
- **Main content**: single scrollable area showing either the **component list** or a **preview/detail** view (one mode at a time when space is limited).
- **Card grid**: list of captured elements as cards; same information hierarchy as extension snippet cards.

## Card design (match extension SnippetCard)

Each card must include:

- **Thumbnail**: top of card; fixed height (e.g. ~100px); image or placeholder; clickable for preview.
- **Meta block**: title (single line, ellipsis), secondary line (e.g. source domain · date or "Captured").
- **Primary actions**: at least **Insert** (primary) and **Preview**; same clarity and labeling style as extension ("Copy HTML", "Copy JSX", "Preview").
- **Visual style**: border, radius, padding, and hover state aligned with extension (tokens: `--color-border`, `--radius-2`, `--space-*`, `--shadow-md` on hover).

Use the same 3-layer token model (primitive → semantic → component). Do not hardcode colors or spacing in card internals.

## Search and filter

- Search input: same behavior as extension library (filter by name/source); same token-based styling as extension search (e.g. `library-search` look and feel).
- Optional: filters (e.g. by date, source) if they exist in the extension; keep parity.

## Empty and loading states

- Empty state: when there are no elements, match extension empty state tone and layout (message + optional CTA).
- Loading: show loader for any operation over ~200ms; avoid blocking the whole UI.

## Typography and spacing

- Use shared baseline: primary text, muted text, caption; spacing scale 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32; radius scale 4, 8, 12, 16.
- Card gap and internal padding should feel consistent with extension library grid (e.g. gap ~12px, card padding ~12px).

## Interaction quality

- Immediate feedback on click (Insert, Preview).
- Loaders for async work; target interaction latency under ~100ms where possible.
- Keyboard support and accessible labels for icon-only buttons, per shared accessibility baseline.

---

# FigmaConstraint: Plugin iframe dimensions

Plugin UI runs in an iframe with fixed dimensions (e.g. width 360, height 500–600). Content must fit without horizontal scroll; use vertical scroll for the list. Card grid may be single-column or two-column depending on width; prefer two-column when width allows (match extension popup library density where possible).

---

# FigmaConstraint: No capture overlay

The plugin does not have a page overlay or capture flow; only library list, preview, and insert. Do not replicate extension overlay styles unless adding a future in-Figma capture feature.

---

# Parity Checklist (Before Finalizing Plugin UI)

- [ ] Header + search + main list structure matches extension library intent.
- [ ] Card layout: thumbnail, title, meta, Insert + Preview (and any secondary actions) match extension snippet card hierarchy and tokens.
- [ ] Shared token architecture and visual baseline (colors, typography, spacing, radius) are used; no hardcoded values in component internals.
- [ ] Empty and loading states align with extension library.
- [ ] Any divergence is marked with `FigmaConstraint` and reason.
- [ ] Accessibility baseline from shared rule is preserved.
